Values for ntm, read by `ntm:conventions`. Shown only when a person invokes this skill directly.

Each section is read by heading. Every line is something you agreed to during setup; a line that is missing means its default. Prose is fine: say what you do in your own words.

## About you

- Name: <!-- how a message title addresses you -->
- Timezone: <!-- IANA zone, e.g. America/Chicago. Every date in the system is computed in it -->
- Country and currency: <!-- for price watch, e.g. US, USD -->

## Board

- Backend: <!-- linear | claude-docs | describe your own below -->
- Board name: <!-- the team, doc, project or workspace that holds every ticket, as the backend names it -->
- Board id: <!-- if the backend needs one for lookups; blank otherwise -->
- Ticket prefix: <!-- e.g. HOME for HOME-12; blank where ids carry none -->
- Statuses — the board's real names for each class:
  - plannable: <!-- usually three: a backlog, a to-do and an in-progress status -->
  - started: <!-- which of the plannable statuses means work has begun -->
  - blocked: <!-- open, but you can't move it right now; blank if the board has none -->
  - done:
  - canceled:
  - duplicate:
- Price watch project: <!-- the project whose tickets are purchases waiting for a good price; blank = price watch off -->
- Notes — the title of each note the system keeps:
  - pauses: Pauses
  - message history: Message history
  - grooming log: Grooming log
  - price watch stores: Price watch stores
  - Amazon alert steps: Amazon alert steps

