## Labels

The real name on your board for each label the system uses.

- Ticket labels:
  - no-autoschedule: no-autoschedule
  - pending-shipment: pending-shipment
  - has-amazon-alert: has-amazon-alert
  - amazon-unavailable: amazon-unavailable
- Project labels (tickets inherit them):
  - price-watch: price-watch
  - no-autoschedule: no-autoschedule

## Planning

How the planner works your board. Read by `ntm:plan`, the planner agent and the weekly planning.

- Rhythm: one task per weekday <!-- or: one per day; two per weekday; whatever you keep up with -->
- Planning days: weekdays <!-- the days that get a task automatically -->
- Plans ahead: one week <!-- how far the weekly planning plans: one week (Monday to Friday); two weeks; the month -->
- Sizing: Fibonacci points; 1 finishes in a night, 2 is iffy for one evening, 3 or more is multi-day <!-- what an estimate means on your board; the planner guesses from the title when a ticket has none -->
- A day's worth: about an hour <!-- what the planner aims for when it picks -->
- Never picks: no-autoschedule, pending-shipment, blocked status <!-- the exclusions, each checked on the ticket and its ancestors -->
- Parents: plan the open sub-tickets, never the parent
- Weekly message: what got done, what's still open, the week ahead <!-- the halves the weekly planning message carries -->

<!-- Anything else about how you want planning done, as you'd say it: "nothing heavy on Fridays", "garage work only on weekends". -->

## Shopping

How the price watch judges a deal. Read by `ntm:price-watch` and the shopper agent.

- Condition: new <!-- unless a ticket says otherwise -->
- Delivery: online only, to your country
- A deal: at or near the ticket's target, or well below the usual price <!-- what gets you an alert -->

<!-- Anything else about how you shop: stores you always or never use are kept in the price watch stores note; say here what counts beyond that. -->

